 "notes": {
  "j1": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 300,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 1\nFirst-time setup\n\nA rider gives their preferences: places, usual times, days and ride type, then sees a sample ping before allowing notifications.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "gray"
  },
  "j2": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 1400,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 2\nCommute ping: start earlier\n\nA set-up rider gets the ping 45 minutes before their usual time, opens the app, and books at the advised start time.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "blue"
  },
  "j3": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 2500,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 3\nCommute ping: pause or mute\n\nThe rider stops pings for today, or mutes one commute, from the notification or from Account > Commute alerts (also reachable from the bell on home), and can undo it there.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "purple"
  },
  "j4": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 3600,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 4\nNormal home: no commute due\n\nOutside a rider's commute window (from 45 minutes before to 30 minutes after a usual time), and for riders who have not set up, the home screen is the normal one: search, Later and recent places. The forecast appears once a destination is entered.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "gray"
  },
  "j5": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 4700,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 5\nHome inside the commute window\n\nOnly a set-up rider, and only from 45 minutes before to 30 minutes after their usual time, sees the forecast card and ride-type chips for their usual ride type. Everyone else sees Journey 4.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "orange"
  },
  "j6": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 5800,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 6\nPickup shift at a house\n\nIn surge, a single-entry place gets one cheaper pickup point: the nearest 7 to 10 min walk, on the way to the drop. The rider books from it, or taps Not now.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "green"
  },
  "j7": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 6900,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 7\nPickup shift at a station\n\nA multi-gate place asks for the gate first, then opens one cheaper-gate suggestion if there is one.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "teal"
  },
  "j8": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 8000,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 8\nNo suggestion shown\n\nShort trips and normal-price times get the normal ride options, with no pickup suggestion.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "gray"
  },
  "j9": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 9100,
   "w": 440,
   "text": "JOURNEY 9\nPickup shift at a small shop\n\nWith few gates or pickup points, such as standing in front of a small shop, the same rules apply: in surge, one cheaper spot nearby can be suggested.",
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "green"
  },
  "j10": {
   "x": -520,
   "y": 10200,
   "w": 440,
   "size": "md",
   "bold": false,
   "fill": "yellow",
   "text": "JOURNEY 10\nDriver rule for alternate pickups\n\nSpecification only, not in the prototype. Only drivers who do not have to cross the surge hotspot see the request: outside it on the destination side, or within 500 m of its edge. If nobody accepts in 10 minutes, it opens to all drivers."
  }
 }
}